{
  "schema": "loom.runtime_profile/1",
  "domain": "settings_fields",
  "revision": 4,
  "description": "Settings field traits (type, has_default, description, values) and the vocabulary of edit labels, plus the human layer (M1-D0): `groups` (the eight human groups with subgroups, id -> {label, why, order, subgroups}), `human` on every field (label, why, effect in pl and en; levels of the scopes chain where it may be set; group/subgroup; role; flows that read it; technical_only) and `profile_values` (values of runtime profiles shown as fields with the chip 'runtime profile: <domain>', never copied into config). Grouping is data: an overlay may regroup, rename or hide (view kind settings_groups in graph_views.pack); the technical key stays under 'technical name' and no field is ever dropped. The edit rules of the fields are general rules {scope, target, action, effect} in the one rule store, runtime/action_rules.pack (target kind settings_field, action edit); no matching rule = allow. Effects map a rule effect to the edit label shown; an unknown effect passes through as its own label (open string). Default values are read from the real defaults (config_defaults / loom_config_defaults), never copied into the pack. Review of M1-D0 (rev. 3): `human.levels` = the levels where a reader honours the value, backed by `level_evidence` (chain-resolved keys, per-request wire options); a field whose key no code reads yet carries `status {state: planned, by, reason}`; `values_open` marks an example list; `human.role_status` keeps a role chip honest until ports.pack knows the role; the `group` and `levels` enums are gone (an overlay may add a group of its own; levels are checked against the live scope chain). Review fixes (rev. 4): `values[].on_set` and `on_unlisted` say what a write of a planned or unlisted value does on every write path (refuse: its reader rejects it; warn: stored with a warning); `level_evidence.installation` backs the installation level (a profile value is set only in its profile, never in config.json); `placement` lets an overlay move one field into another group without copying the fields array; a missing `human` is a listed problem, not a load failure; `human.flows` are checked against the action catalogue.",
  "defaults": {
    "element_class": "settings_field",
    "rule_action": "edit",
    "rule_scope": "installation",
    "effects": [
      {
        "id": "allow",
        "edit": "optional",
        "label_pl": "fakultatywna",
        "enforced": false,
        "meaning": "Default when no rule matches (a block needs an initiator): the field may be left empty or changed freely."
      },
      {
        "id": "require_value",
        "edit": "required",
        "label_pl": "obligatoryjna",
        "enforced": false,
        "meaning": "A feature does not work until the field is set; deleting it is not blocked."
      },
      {
        "id": "deny",
        "edit": "read_only",
        "label_pl": "tylko_odczyt",
        "enforced": true,
        "meaning": "Maintained by Loom; writes through config APIs are rejected."
      },
      {
        "id": "require_confirmation",
        "edit": "requires_confirmation",
        "label_pl": "wymaga_potwierdzenia",
        "enforced": false,
        "meaning": "A change that raises consumption needs the user's explicit confirmation; enforced by the owning action, not by the generic write."
      }
    ],
    "groups": {
      "ty": {
        "label": {
          "pl": "Ty",
          "en": "You"
        },
        "why": {
          "pl": "Kim jesteś dla aplikacji: jak ma do Ciebie mówić i co o Tobie dokłada do żądania.",
          "en": "Who you are to the app: how it talks to you and what about you goes with a request."
        },
        "order": 1,
        "subgroups": [
          {
            "id": "profil",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Profil",
              "en": "Profile"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Opis Ciebie zebrany w wywiadzie lub formularzu.",
              "en": "The description of you gathered in the interview or the form."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "reguly",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Reguły o Tobie",
              "en": "Rules about you"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "To, co strażnik rozmowy zapamiętał o Tobie i wysyła z żądaniem.",
              "en": "What the conversation guardian remembered about you and sends with a request."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "rozmowa": {
        "label": {
          "pl": "Rozmowa",
          "en": "Conversation"
        },
        "why": {
          "pl": "Jak powstaje odpowiedź: który model, jak długo, jak swobodnie i którą drogą.",
          "en": "How a reply is made: which model, how long, how freely and by which route."
        },
        "order": 2,
        "subgroups": [
          {
            "id": "polecenia",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Polecenia z rozmowy",
              "en": "Commands from the chat"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Co dzieje się, gdy to, co piszesz, jest poleceniem, a nie wiadomością.",
              "en": "What happens when what you type is a command, not a message."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "agent",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Agent",
              "en": "Agent"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Ile model może zrobić sam, gdy pracuje narzędziami.",
              "en": "How much the model may do alone when it works with tools."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "modele": {
        "label": {
          "pl": "Modele",
          "en": "Models"
        },
        "why": {
          "pl": "Skąd biorą się modele, kto wykonuje którą pracę i jakimi kluczami.",
          "en": "Where the models come from, who does which job and with which keys."
        },
        "order": 3,
        "subgroups": [
          {
            "id": "dostawca",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Dostawca",
              "en": "Provider"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Usługa, do której idą wywołania modeli, i jej klucz.",
              "en": "The service the model calls go to, and its key."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "role",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Role",
              "en": "Roles"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Który model wykonuje którą pracę: rozmowa, analiza w tle, strażnik, obraz, głos.",
              "en": "Which model does which job: conversation, background analysis, guardian, image, voice."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "klucze",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Klucze dostępu",
              "en": "Access keys"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Klucze do osobnych usług (mowa, tekst ze zdjęcia, analiza zbiorcza); nigdy nie pokazywane.",
              "en": "Keys to separate services (speech, text from an image, batch analysis); never shown."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "kontekst": {
        "label": {
          "pl": "Kontekst",
          "en": "Context"
        },
        "why": {
          "pl": "Co z Twoich rozmów, pamięci i grafu trafia do modelu razem z wiadomością, i jak to powstaje w tle.",
          "en": "What of your conversations, memory and graph reaches the model with a message, and how it is made in the background."
        },
        "order": 4,
        "subgroups": [
          {
            "id": "wybor",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Co trafia do modelu",
              "en": "What reaches the model"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Ile i w jakiej kolejności dokłada się do żądania.",
              "en": "How much goes with a request and in which order."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "analiza",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Analiza w tle",
              "en": "Background analysis"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Czytanie wiadomości w tle, z którego powstaje graf wiedzy.",
              "en": "Reading messages in the background, which builds the knowledge graph."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "straznik",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Strażnik rozmowy",
              "en": "Conversation guardian"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Sekretarz, który zauważa poprawki i doprecyzowania i nigdy nie zmienia Twoich wiadomości.",
              "en": "The secretary that notices corrections and clarifications and never changes your messages."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "pamiec",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Pamięć z folderu",
              "en": "Memory from a folder"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Ile z plików folderu dodanego do pamięci jest czytane.",
              "en": "How much of a folder added to memory is read."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "slad",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Ślad „Co wysłaliśmy”",
              "en": "The “What we sent” trail"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Zapis tego, co dokładnie poszło do modelu przy każdej wiadomości.",
              "en": "The record of what exactly went to the model with each message."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "interfejs": {
        "label": {
          "pl": "Interfejs",
          "en": "Interface"
        },
        "why": {
          "pl": "Jak aplikacja wygląda i co pokazuje: motyw, język, animacje, ekran czatu, nawigator grafu.",
          "en": "How the app looks and what it shows: theme, language, animations, chat screen, graph navigator."
        },
        "order": 5,
        "subgroups": [
          {
            "id": "wyglad",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Wygląd i start",
              "en": "Look and start"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Motyw, język i to, co otwiera się na początku.",
              "en": "Theme, language and what opens first."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "animacje",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Animacje",
              "en": "Animations"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Jak poruszają się elementy ekranu.",
              "en": "How the screen elements move."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "czat",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Ekran czatu",
              "en": "Chat screen"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Co widać wokół wiadomości i pola pisania.",
              "en": "What is shown around the messages and the composer."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "nawigator",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Nawigator grafu",
              "en": "Graph navigator"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Jak rysuje się graf: lista, mapa, ile węzłów na raz.",
              "en": "How the graph is drawn: list, map, how many nodes at once."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "strony",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Strony i okna",
              "en": "Pages and windows"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Po ile wiadomości i węzłów ładuje się na raz; nic nie jest tracone.",
              "en": "How many messages and nodes load at once; nothing is lost."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "prywatnosc": {
        "label": {
          "pl": "Prywatność",
          "en": "Privacy"
        },
        "why": {
          "pl": "Co wychodzi z urządzenia, do kogo, i co chroni Twoje pliki.",
          "en": "What leaves the device, to whom, and what protects your files."
        },
        "order": 6,
        "subgroups": [
          {
            "id": "dane",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Co wychodzi z urządzenia",
              "en": "What leaves the device"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Klucze w rozmowie, pytania systemu o foldery, zewnętrzne źródła narzędzi.",
              "en": "Keys in the chat, system questions about folders, external tool sources."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "synchronizacja",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Synchronizacja",
              "en": "Sync"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Repozytorium, z którym wymieniasz dane, i jego token.",
              "en": "The repository you exchange data with, and its token."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "bezpieczenstwo",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Bezpieczeństwo plików",
              "en": "File safety"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Ochrona przed złośliwymi archiwami i obcym kodem z repozytorium.",
              "en": "Protection from malicious archives and foreign code from a repository."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "porzadki",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Porządki",
              "en": "Housekeeping"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Co silnik sprząta przy starcie; nic, do czego coś się odwołuje, nie ginie.",
              "en": "What the engine tidies at start; nothing that is referenced is lost."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "koszty": {
        "label": {
          "pl": "Koszty",
          "en": "Costs"
        },
        "why": {
          "pl": "Twoje limity wydatków, strażnik wzrostu zużycia ×10 i księga tego, ile wydałeś.",
          "en": "Your spending limits, the ×10 consumption growth guard and the ledger of what you spent."
        },
        "order": 7,
        "subgroups": [
          {
            "id": "limity",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Limity wydatków",
              "en": "Spending limits"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Progi, po których aplikacja pyta, odmawia albo powiadamia.",
              "en": "Thresholds after which the app asks, refuses or notifies."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "ksiega",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Księga zużycia",
              "en": "Usage ledger"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Jak zapisuje się i porządkuje historię zużycia.",
              "en": "How the usage history is recorded and tidied."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "silnik": {
        "label": {
          "pl": "Silnik",
          "en": "Engine"
        },
        "why": {
          "pl": "Wnętrze aplikacji: indeksy, dziennik zdarzeń, wątki zadań — i tabela wszystkich pól pod nazwami technicznymi.",
          "en": "The inside of the app: indexes, the event log, task threads — and the table of every field under its technical name."
        },
        "order": 8,
        "subgroups": [
          {
            "id": "indeks",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Indeksy i dziennik",
              "en": "Indexes and log"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Jak buduje się indeks wyszukiwania i co trafia do dziennika zdarzeń.",
              "en": "How the search index is built and what goes to the event log."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "zadania",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Zadania w tle",
              "en": "Background tasks"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Ile prac w tle idzie naraz.",
              "en": "How many background jobs run at once."
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "wszystkie",
            "label": {
              "pl": "Wszystkie pola",
              "en": "All fields"
            },
            "why": {
              "pl": "Każde pole pod nazwą techniczną, także te, których nie ma w grupach po ludzku.",
              "en": "Every field under its technical name, including those the human groups do not list."
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "placement": {},
    "level_evidence": {
      "chain": [
        "default_model",
        "semantic_model",
        "guardian_model",
        "chat_representation",
        "chat_thread_filter",
        "guardian_person_rules",
        "chat_flow",
        "extrapolation_preset",
        "extrapolation_bounds",
        "action_result_target"
      ],
      "turn": [
        "default_model",
        "temperature",
        "max_tokens",
        "system_prompt",
        "stream",
        "graph_memory_depth",
        "chat_flow",
        "chat_reasoning",
        "chat_context_order"
      ],
      "installation": [
        "default_model",
        "semantic_model",
        "guardian_model",
        "chat_representation",
        "chat_thread_filter",
        "guardian_person_rules",
        "chat_flow",
        "extrapolation_preset",
        "extrapolation_bounds",
        "action_result_target",
        "worker/batch_threshold",
        "worker/analysis_modes",
        "graph_memory/default_depth",
        "graph_memory/default_max_nodes",
        "chat_context/context_order"
      ]
    },
    "fields": [
      {
        "key": "base_url",
        "scope": "config",
        "group": "chat",
        "type": "string",
        "has_default": true,
        "description": "Base URL of the OpenAI-compatible chat API (OpenRouter by default).",
        "human": {
          "label": {
            "pl": "Adres usługi modeli",
            "en": "Model service address"
          },
          "why": {
            "pl": "Dokąd aplikacja wysyła rozmowy; domyślnie OpenRouter, który daje dostęp do wielu modeli jednym kluczem.",
            "en": "Where the app sends conversations; OpenRouter by default, which reaches many models with one key."
          },
          "effect": {
            "pl": "Zmiana adresu kieruje wszystkie wywołania modeli (czat, analiza, osadzenia) do innej usługi zgodnej z OpenAI.",
            "en": "Changing the address sends every model call (chat, analysis, embeddings) to another OpenAI-compatible service."
          },
          "levels": [
            "person"
          ],
          "group": "modele",
          "subgroup": "dostawca",
          "flows": [
            "chat.send",
            "semantic.analyse",
            "semantic.batch",
            "agent.run",
            "use_model",
            "embedding.embed"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "default_model",
        "scope": "config",
        "group": "chat",
        "type": "string",
        "has_default": true,
        "description": "Model used for chat when a request names none.",
        "human": {
          "label": {
            "pl": "Model rozmowy",
            "en": "Conversation model"
          },
          "why": {
            "pl": "Który model odpowiada w czacie, gdy rozmowa ani wiadomość nie wskazują innego.",
            "en": "Which model answers in the chat when neither the conversation nor the message names another."
          },
          "effect": {
            "pl": "Nowe odpowiedzi przychodzą z wybranego modelu; trwające się nie zmieniają. Rozmowa lub projekt mogą mieć własny model.",
            "en": "New replies come from the chosen model; replies in progress do not change. A conversation or project may have its own model."
          },
          "levels": [
            "installation",
            "person",
            "project",
            "conversation",
            "turn"
          ],
          "group": "rozmowa",
          "role": "chat.default",
          "flows": [
            "chat.send",
            "actions.run",
            "agent.run",
            "actions.preview"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "llm_provider",
        "scope": "config",
        "group": "chat",
        "type": "string",
        "has_default": false,
        "description": "Which model provider answers the chat and the other model calls: openrouter (preset), local (an OpenAI-compatible server on this device, such as llama.cpp or Ollama, at local_model_base_url), or the id of any provider manifest you added. Default: openrouter.",
        "human": {
          "label": {
            "pl": "Dostawca modeli",
            "en": "Model provider"
          },
          "why": {
            "pl": "Czy modele obsługuje OpenRouter (preset), serwer na tym urządzeniu (np. llama.cpp, Ollama), czy dostawca, którego sam dodałeś.",
            "en": "Whether OpenRouter (preset), a server on this device (llama.cpp, Ollama) or a provider you added serves the models."
          },
          "effect": {
            "pl": "Wszystkie wywołania modeli idą do wskazanego dostawcy; przy „local” adres bierze się z pola Adres lokalnego serwera modeli.",
            "en": "Every model call goes to the named provider; with “local” the address comes from the Local model server address field."
          },
          "levels": [
            "person"
          ],
          "group": "modele",
          "subgroup": "dostawca",
          "flows": [
            "use_model",
            "chat.send"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "local_model_base_url",
        "scope": "config",
        "group": "chat",
        "type": "string",
        "has_default": false,
        "description": "Address of the model server on this device for llm_provider = local: an OpenAI-compatible API, such as http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1 for llama.cpp or http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1 for Ollama. No key is sent. Default: http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1.",
        "human": {
          "label": {
            "pl": "Adres lokalnego serwera modeli",
            "en": "Local model server address"
          },
          "why": {
            "pl": "Gdzie na tym urządzeniu działa serwer modeli, gdy dostawcą jest „local” (np. http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1).",
            "en": "Where the model server runs on this device when the provider is “local” (e.g. http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1)."
          },
          "effect": {
            "pl": "Przy dostawcy „local” wywołania modeli trafiają pod ten adres; przy innym dostawcy pole nie ma wpływu.",
            "en": "With the “local” provider model calls go to this address; with another provider the field has no effect."
          },
          "levels": [
            "person"
          ],
          "group": "modele",
          "subgroup": "dostawca",
          "flows": [
            "use_model"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "semantic_model",
        "scope": "config",
        "group": "semantic",
        "type": "string",
        "has_default": true,
        "description": "Model for background semantic analysis; empty string disables the LLM path (regex fallback).",
        "human": {
          "label": {
            "pl": "Model analizy w tle",
            "en": "Background analysis model"
          },
          "why": {
            "pl": "Który tani model czyta wiadomości w tle i wyciąga z nich tematy, encje i powiązania do grafu; pusty = tylko lokalne reguły, bez kosztu.",
            "en": "Which cheap model reads messages in the background and pulls topics, entities and relations into the graph; empty = local rules only, no cost."
          },
          "effect": {
            "pl": "Z modelem analiza jest dokładniejsza i płatna; bez niego graf buduje się z lokalnych reguł. Model wskazany w rozmowie lub projekcie honoruje dziś tylko strażnik rozmowy; analiza w tle bierze Twój.",
            "en": "With a model the analysis is more accurate and paid; without one the graph is built from local rules. A model named in a conversation or project is honoured today only by the conversation guardian; the background analysis takes yours."
          },
          "levels": [
            "installation",
            "person",
            "project",
            "conversation"
          ],
          "group": "modele",
          "subgroup": "role",
          "role": "analysis.fast",
          "flows": [
            "semantic.analyse",
            "semantic.batch",
            "guardian.observe",
            "actions.preview"
          ],
          "technical_only": true
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "temperature",
        "scope": "config",
        "group": "chat",
        "type": "number",
        "has_default": true,
        "description": "Sampling temperature for chat completions.",
        "human": {
          "label": {
            "pl": "Temperatura (swoboda odpowiedzi)",
            "en": "Temperature (reply freedom)"
          },
          "why": {
            "pl": "Ile losowości ma odpowiedź: niżej = powtarzalniej i ostrożniej, wyżej = swobodniej i bardziej twórczo.",
            "en": "How much randomness a reply has: lower = more repeatable and careful, higher = freer and more creative."
          },
          "effect": {
            "pl": "Działa od następnej odpowiedzi; dotyczy czatu, analizy w tle i agenta.",
            "en": "Applies from the next reply; covers the chat, the background analysis and the agent."
          },
          "levels": [
            "person",
            "turn"
          ],
          "group": "rozmowa",
          "flows": [
            "chat.send",
            "semantic.analyse",
            "agent.run",
            "archive.run"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "max_tokens",
        "scope": "config",
        "group": "chat",
        "type": "integer",
        "has_default": true,
        "description": "Completion token limit sent with chat requests.",
        "human": {
          "label": {
            "pl": "Maksymalna długość odpowiedzi",
            "en": "Maximum reply length"
          },
          "why": {
            "pl": "Górna granica długości jednej odpowiedzi (w tokenach, mniej więcej 3/4 słowa każdy); długie odpowiedzi kosztują więcej.",
            "en": "The upper bound of one reply's length (in tokens, roughly 3/4 of a word each); long replies cost more."
          },
          "effect": {
            "pl": "Odpowiedź dłuższa niż limit urywa się na granicy; wyższy limit = dłuższe i droższe odpowiedzi.",
            "en": "A reply longer than the limit stops at the bound; a higher limit = longer and dearer replies."
          },
          "levels": [
            "person",
            "turn"
          ],
          "group": "rozmowa",
          "flows": [
            "chat.send",
            "agent.run",
            "semantic.analyse",
            "actions.preview",
            "archive.run"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "theme",
        "scope": "config",
        "group": "ui",
        "type": "string",
        "has_default": true,
        "description": "UI theme preset name (dark, amoled).",
        "human": {
          "label": {
            "pl": "Motyw",
            "en": "Theme"
          },
          "why": {
            "pl": "Wygląd aplikacji: ciemny albo AMOLED (czarny, oszczędza baterię na ekranach OLED).",
            "en": "The app's look: dark or AMOLED (black, saves battery on OLED screens)."
          },
          "effect": {
            "pl": "Zmiana działa od razu na tym urządzeniu.",
            "en": "The change applies at once on this device."
          },
          "levels": [
            "person"
          ],
          "group": "interfejs",
          "subgroup": "wyglad",
          "flows": []
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "start_view",
        "scope": "config",
        "group": "ui",
        "type": "array",
        "has_default": false,
        "description": "What the app opens to, as an ordered list tried first to last; the first that yields a view wins (the preset is [last_saved, last_conversation, new_conversation]): last_saved = the view you left (layout and conversation, kept on this device), last_conversation = the most recently updated conversation, new_conversation = an empty chat (always possible, so the app always opens to a chat). A single string is a list of one. Unknown names are skipped. Default: the preset (R56).",
        "human": {
          "label": {
            "pl": "Co otwiera się na starcie",
            "en": "What opens at start"
          },
          "why": {
            "pl": "Kolejność prób przy starcie: ostatni widok, ostatnia rozmowa, nowa rozmowa — pierwsza możliwa wygrywa.",
            "en": "The order tried at start: the last view, the last conversation, a new conversation — the first possible one wins."
          },
          "effect": {
            "pl": "Działa przy następnym uruchomieniu; nowa rozmowa jest zawsze możliwa, więc aplikacja zawsze otwiera czat.",
            "en": "Applies at the next launch; a new conversation is always possible, so the app always opens to a chat."
          },
          "levels": [
            "person"
          ],
          "group": "interfejs",
          "subgroup": "wyglad",
          "flows": []
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "layout_mode",
        "scope": "config",
        "group": "ui",
        "type": "string",
        "has_default": false,
        "values": [
          {
            "value": "full_screen_chat",
            "preset": true,
            "meaning": {
              "pl": "Czat na pełnym ekranie (preset).",
              "en": "Full-screen chat (the preset)."
            }
          },
          {
            "value": "views_grid",
            "meaning": {
              "pl": "Warsztat: siatka widoków aplikacji.",
              "en": "The workbench: a grid of the application's views."
            }
          },
          {
            "value": "windows",
            "status": "planned",
            "reason": {
              "pl": "Okna pływające i dokowane to następny wątek po P20; do tego czasu otwiera się warsztat (siatka widoków).",
              "en": "Floating and dockable windows are the next thread after P20; until then the workbench (views_grid) opens."
            },
            "meaning": {
              "pl": "Okna pływające i dokowane (planowane; do tego czasu otwiera się warsztat).",
              "en": "Floating and docked windows (planned; until then the workbench opens)."
            },
            "on_set": "warn"
          }
        ],
        "description": "Layout of the application: full_screen_chat (preset: the full-screen standard chat app, profile \"Czat\"), views_grid (the workbench: application views grid, profile \"Warsztat\") or windows (floating and dockable windows; planned, not implemented yet: until it is, the workbench opens). The ⋮ menu switches between them for the session; the last choice is part of last_saved. Default: full_screen_chat (R56).",
        "human": {
          "label": {
            "pl": "Układ aplikacji",
            "en": "Application layout"
          },
          "why": {
            "pl": "Czat na pełnym ekranie (preset), warsztat z siatką widoków albo okna (planowane, jeszcze nie gotowe).",
            "en": "Full-screen chat (preset), the workbench with a grid of views, or windows (planned, not ready yet)."
          },
          "effect": {
            "pl": "Zmienia układ od razu; „okna” jeszcze nie działają — wtedy otwiera się warsztat, z powodem.",
            "en": "Changes the layout at once; “windows” does not work yet — then the workbench opens, with the reason."
          },
          "levels": [
            "person"
          ],
          "group": "interfejs",
          "subgroup": "wyglad",
          "flows": []
        },
        "on_unlisted": "warn"
      },
      {
        "key": "animation_styles",
        "scope": "config",
        "group": "ui",
        "section": "Interfejs i wyświetlanie",
        "subsection": "Animacje",
        "type": "object",
        "has_default": false,
        "description": "Your own animation styles, an overlay on the shipped ones (runtime/ui_animation.pack: none, fade, slide, grow, scale, grow+fade): {name: {kind: none|fade|slide|grow|scale|grow+fade, direction?: left|right|up|down, duration: {value, unit: ms|s|frames}, easing: a named easing or a cubic-bezier(...)}}. A style of the same name replaces the shipped one. Default: none (only the shipped styles).",
        "human": {
          "label": {
            "pl": "Własne style animacji",
            "en": "Your own animation styles"
          },
          "why": {
            "pl": "Twoje własne style ruchu (zanikanie, wsunięcie, wzrost…) obok wbudowanych.",
            "en": "Your own motion styles (fade, slide, grow…) beside the builtin ones."
          },
          "effect": {
            "pl": "Nowy styl można potem przypisać elementom w polu Animacje elementów; wbudowane zostają.",
            "en": "A new style can then be assigned to elements in the Element animations field; the builtin ones stay."
          },
          "levels": [
            "person"
          ],
          "group": "interfejs",
          "subgroup": "animacje",
          "flows": []
        }
      },
      {
