      {
        "key": "chat_context_order",
        "scope": "config",
        "group": "context",
        "type": "string",
        "has_default": false,
        "description": "Order of the context sections of a chat request, a name from the runtime profile chat_context (orders, with the user's profile overlay): legacy (system, memory, graph, project, history; the profile's preset) or stable_first (system, memory, project, history, graph: the stable sections first so a provider's prompt cache hits), or any order the user adds to profiles/chat_context.pack. The listed values are that profile's orders (values_from), so a write refuses only a name the effective profile does not know. Empty = the profile's context_order. A request may name its own order (option context_order). Default: none (the profile's preset).",
        "values": [
          {
            "value": "",
            "meaning": {
              "pl": "Puste: kolejność z ustawień domyślnych (preset).",
              "en": "Empty: the order from the default settings (the preset)."
            }
          },
          {
            "value": "legacy",
            "meaning": {
              "pl": "Klasycznie: instrukcja, pamięć, graf, projekt, historia (preset profilu).",
              "en": "Classic: instruction, memory, graph, project, history (the profile's preset)."
            }
          },
          {
            "value": "stable_first",
            "meaning": {
              "pl": "Najpierw części stałe: instrukcja, pamięć, projekt, historia, graf.",
              "en": "Stable parts first: instruction, memory, project, history, graph."
            }
          },
          {
            "value": "stability",
            "status": "planned",
            "reason": {
              "pl": "M1-D2 dopisze kolejność „według stabilności” [instrukcja, profil, reguły, pamięć, projekt, historia, graf]; do tego czasu czat odrzuca tę nazwę przy następnym żądaniu („unknown context_order”).",
              "en": "M1-D2 adds the order stability [system, profile, rules, memory, project, history, graph] to chat_context.pack; until then chat_engine rejects the name with 'unknown context_order'."
            },
            "meaning": {
              "pl": "Według stabilności: instrukcja, profil, reguły, pamięć, projekt, historia, graf (planowane, M1-D2).",
              "en": "By stability: instruction, profile, rules, memory, project, history, graph (planned, M1-D2)."
            },
            "on_set": "refuse"
          }
        ],
        "values_from": {
          "profile": "chat_context",
          "pointer": "/orders",
          "keys": true
        },
        "human": {
          "label": {
            "pl": "Kolejność części żądania",
            "en": "Order of the request parts"
          },
          "why": {
            "pl": "W jakiej kolejności model dostaje instrukcję, pamięć, graf, projekt i historię: klasycznie (preset profilu) albo najpierw części stałe, żeby pamięć podręczna dostawcy trafiała częściej.",
            "en": "In which order the model gets the instruction, memory, graph, project and history: classic (the profile's preset) or the stable parts first so the provider's prompt cache hits more often."
          },
          "effect": {
            "pl": "Ta sama treść w innej kolejności; gdy najpierw idą części stałe, powtarzające się żądania bywają tańsze. Puste = kolejność z pola „Kolejność części żądania (preset profilu)”.",
            "en": "The same content in another order; with the stable parts first, repeated requests tend to be cheaper. Empty = the order of the field “Order of the request parts (profile preset)”."
          },
          "levels": [
            "person",
            "turn"
          ],
          "group": "kontekst",
          "subgroup": "wybor",
          "flows": [
            "chat.send"
          ]
        },
        "on_unlisted": "refuse"
      },
      {
        "key": "language",
        "scope": "config",
        "group": "ui",
        "type": "string",
        "has_default": false,
        "description": "Language of the notes the chat flow adds to a reply (an emergent element note, an invalid graph reply note): a language code with texts in the data (pl, en). Empty = en. The shell labels follow ui_language. Default: none (en).",
        "human": {
          "label": {
            "pl": "Język dopisków aplikacji",
            "en": "Language of the app's notes"
          },
          "why": {
            "pl": "W jakim języku aplikacja dopisuje swoje uwagi w odpowiedziach (np. „element nieznany”, „odpowiedź w złym formacie”): pl albo en; pusty = en.",
            "en": "In which language the app adds its own notes to replies (e.g. “unknown element”, “reply in the wrong format”): pl or en; empty = en."
          },
          "effect": {
            "pl": "Napisy menu mają własne pole (Język interfejsu); odpowiedzi modelu nie są tłumaczone.",
            "en": "The menu labels have their own field (Interface language); model replies are not translated."
          },
          "levels": [
            "person"
          ],
          "group": "interfejs",
          "subgroup": "wyglad",
          "flows": [
            "chat.send",
            "graph_native.reply"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "model_capabilities",
        "scope": "config",
        "group": "chat",
        "type": "object",
        "has_default": false,
        "description": "Your own capability overrides per model: {model id: {capability: value}}, layered over the adapter's and the provider manifest's capabilities when a request is checked (use_model, the agent loop, the context format). Nothing is substituted silently: a request a model cannot serve is rejected with the reason before anything is sent. Default: none.",
        "human": {
          "label": {
            "pl": "Własne możliwości modeli",
            "en": "Your own model capabilities"
          },
          "why": {
            "pl": "Co umie dany model (obrazy, narzędzia, format odpowiedzi…) według Ciebie, ponad to, co mówią adapter i manifest dostawcy.",
            "en": "What a given model can do (images, tools, response format…) according to you, over what the adapter and the provider manifest say."
          },
          "effect": {
            "pl": "Żądanie, którego model według tych danych nie obsłuży, jest odrzucane z powodem, zanim cokolwiek zostanie wysłane.",
            "en": "A request the model cannot serve according to these data is rejected with the reason before anything is sent."
          },
          "levels": [
            "person"
          ],
          "group": "modele",
          "subgroup": "dostawca",
          "flows": [
            "use_model",
            "chat.send",
            "agent.run"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "provider_manifests",
        "scope": "config",
        "group": "chat",
        "type": "array",
        "has_default": false,
        "description": "Provider manifests you added, each in the ProviderManifest shape (id, adapter, base URL, capabilities, secret key name), loaded beside the builtin ones at call time so an edit applies to the next call; llm_provider, image_provider and speech_provider name a manifest by its id. Default: none.",
        "human": {
          "label": {
            "pl": "Dodani dostawcy",
            "en": "Added providers"
          },
          "why": {
            "pl": "Twoi dostawcy modeli obok wbudowanych: adres, adapter, możliwości i nazwa klucza; wskazujesz ich w polach dostawcy modeli, obrazów i mowy.",
            "en": "Your model providers beside the builtin ones: address, adapter, capabilities and key name; the provider fields for models, images and speech name them."
          },
          "effect": {
            "pl": "Zmiana działa przy następnym wywołaniu modelu; wbudowani dostawcy zostają.",
            "en": "A change applies to the next model call; the builtin providers stay."
          },
          "levels": [
            "person"
          ],
          "group": "modele",
          "subgroup": "dostawca",
          "flows": [
            "use_model",
            "chat.send",
            "providers.list"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "navigator_layout",
